{"name":"Columbia","hex":"#009792","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Columbia","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["America; the United States; an appellation given in honor of Christopher Columbus.","A female personification of the United States."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A breed of sheep developed in the United States."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Columbia"}],"entries":[{"title":"Columbia (personification)","blocks":[{"text":"Columbia, also known as Lady Columbia or Miss Columbia, is a female national personification of the United States. It was also a historical name applied to the Americas and to the New World. The association has given rise to the names of many American places, objects, institutions and companies, including the District of Columbia; Columbia, South Carolina; Columbia University; \"Hail, Columbia\"; Columbia Rediviva; and the Columbia River. Images of the Statue of Liberty largely displaced personified Columbia as the female symbol of the United States by around 1920, and Lady Liberty was seen as both an aspect of Columbia and a rendition of the Goddess of Liberty. She is the central element of the logo of Hollywood film studio Columbia Pictures."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3a/ColumbiaStahrArtwork.jpg/330px-ColumbiaStahrArtwork.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Columbia_(personification)","wikidata":"Q1112443"},{"title":"Columbia University","blocks":[{"text":"Columbia University in the City of New York, commonly referred to as Columbia University, is a private Ivy League research university in New York City, United States. Established in 1754 as King's College by royal charter under George II of Great Britain on the grounds of Trinity Church in Manhattan, it is the oldest institution of higher education in New York and the fifth-oldest in the United States."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/33/Coat_of_Arms_of_Columbia_University.svg/330px-Coat_of_Arms_of_Columbia_University.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Columbia_University","wikidata":"Q49088"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/75/The_Four_Continents_%28America%29%2C_Johann_Joachim_Kaendler_and_assistants%2C_Meissen_Porcelain_Factory%2C_c._1760%2C_hard-paste_porcelain_-_Wadsworth_Atheneum_-_Hartford%2C_CT_-_DSC05373.jpg/500px-thumbnail.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/75/The_Four_Continents_%28America%29%2C_Johann_Joachim_Kaendler_and_assistants%2C_Meissen_Porcelain_Factory%2C_c._1760%2C_hard-paste_porcelain_-_Wadsworth_Atheneum_-_Hartford%2C_CT_-_DSC05373.jpg/1280px-thumbnail.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/75/The_Four_Continents_%28America%29%2C_Johann_Joachim_Kaendler_and_assistants%2C_Meissen_Porcelain_Factory%2C_c._1760%2C_hard-paste_porcelain_-_Wadsworth_Atheneum_-_Hartford%2C_CT_-_DSC05373.jpg/500px-thumbnail.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Personification of the Americas in Meissen porcelain, c. 1760, from a set of the Four Continents","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AThe_Four_Continents_(America)%2C_Johann_Joachim_Kaendler_and_assistants%2C_Meissen_Porcelain_Factory%2C_c._1760%2C_hard-paste_porcelain_-_Wadsworth_Atheneum_-_Hartford%2C_CT_-_DSC05373.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/ff/Uncle_Sam%27s_Thanksgiving_Dinner_%28November_1869%29%2C_by_Thomas_Nast.jpg/500px-Uncle_Sam%27s_Thanksgiving_Dinner_%28November_1869%29%2C_by_Thomas_Nast.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","